The growing adoption of compact electronic devices and embedded computing systems is increasing demand for storage solutions that combine high capacity with efficient space utilization. As electronic manufacturers develop smaller and more integrated products, conventional storage form factors can become difficult to accommodate. Against this backdrop, Ball Grid Array (BGA) solid-state drives are gaining importance across consumer electronics, automotive systems and industrial applications.

